{
	// specializedclasses: class names and descriptions
	"game:characterclass-archivist": "Archivist",
	"game:characterdesc-archivist": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"History is written by the victors. Yes, you see the quill in my hand, don't you? Best watch yourself, then.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Archivists are lorekeepers and archeologists. They can handle cracked vessels and clutter with utmost care, and their attunement to the past lets them ward off temporal instability with ease.",

	"game:characterclass-blackguard": "Blackguard",
	"game:characterdesc-blackguard": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"You need to strike the iron while it's hot? Clearly you're just not hitting it hard enough.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Blackguards are warriors and smiths. They're intimately familiar with weapons and armor, both their creation and their use. They thrive where the fight is, forging their own armaments to carry into battle.",

	"game:characterclass-brickmaker": "Brickmaker",
	"game:characterdesc-brickmaker": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"What do you mean, I've only just scratched the surface? I certainly don't see a need to go any deeper.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Brickmakers are excavators and potters. They can terraform swathes of land with relative ease, claiming all of the earth's bounties. Then they shape the clay they gather into building materials and other useful ceramics.",

	"game:characterclass-butcher": "Butcher",
	"game:characterdesc-butcher": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"The way to the heart is through the stomach. I don't think whoever said that is very familiar with anatomy, but it certainly feels good to keep people fed.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Butchers are cooks and... well, butchers. They know better than anyone how to make the most of a carcass. While they might prefer chopping up beasts, they're equally skilled at harvesting monsters, though they prefer to use the former in their cured meats.",

	"game:characterclass-clockmaker": "Clockmaker",
	"game:characterdesc-clockmaker": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"Measure twice, cut once? Just measure correctly the first time, are you stupid?\"\n</i></font><br><br>Clockmakers are tinkerers and engineers. From intricate mechanisms to massive mechanical power systems, they're always happy to tinker.",

	"game:characterclass-commoner": "Commoner",
	"game:characterdesc-commoner": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"Good enough is good enough, surprisingly.\"\n</i></font><br><br>The Commoner is an odd one out by virtue of being a generalist. Surrounded by true experts, their lack of ambition leaves them unusually efficient in comparison, getting by without needing to worry about food nearly as much as most.",

	"game:characterclass-farmhand": "Farmhand",
	"game:characterdesc-farmhand": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"Yeah, I'd say I'm quite familiar with reaping what I sow. That's… kind of the whole thing I do here. Why do you ask?\"\n</i></font><br><br>Farmhands are cultivators and masters of agriculture. To them, a single patch of wild crop can be the beginning of swathes of grain and vegetables growing from well-fertilized fields, single-handedly providing entire villages with nutrition.",

	"game:characterclass-florist": "Florist",
	"game:characterdesc-florist": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"Why can't I stop and smell the flowers, too? All my bees are doing it…\"\n</i></font><br><br>Florists are beekeepers and herbalists. Eager to keep their allies in good health, they can gather ingredients for simple cures from grass in a pinch. Given time, they can propagate flowers to keep their bees happy, whose honey is used for quality medicine.",

	"game:characterclass-forester": "Forester",
	"game:characterdesc-forester": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"I've never done anything but go against the grain. It's worked out great for me, so why should I stop now?\"\n</i></font><br><br>Foresters are woodcutters and carpenters. They can gather lumber sustainably, getting enough saplings to always replace what they cut down. They always have enough fuel to brave the winters, and what they don't use they carve into useful materials.",

	"game:characterclass-hunter": "Hunter",
	"game:characterdesc-hunter": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"A little birdie told you? Uhm… no, they can't talk. Believe me, I've tried.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Hunters are skilled marksmen and leatherworkers. They take out even the most fearsome predators from a safe distance and expertly process their hides into pelts and leather alike.",

	"game:characterclass-malefactor": "Malefactor",
	"game:characterdesc-malefactor": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"I've got sticky fingers? Duh, it's not like I carry soap around.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Malefactors are merchants and rogues. Often former criminals, their skills have never quite left them. Both wild beasts and monsters seem to nearly ignore them as they delve into ruins to plunder valuable rusty gears and other abandoned resources.",

	"game:characterclass-messenger": "Messenger",
	"game:characterdesc-messenger": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"That arrow nearly hit me! Don't you people know anything!? You're NOT supposed to shoot the messenger!\"\n</i></font><br><br>Messengers are pathfinders and couriers. They lay and maintain roads between points of interest, which they then travel between to run errands like delivering items and spreading notices.",

	"game:characterclass-quarrier": "Quarrier",
	"game:characterdesc-quarrier": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"I don't understand what everybody's complaining about. Moving mountains is easy, just do it one part at a time.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Quarriers are laborers and stonemasons. They smash through rock with heavy hands, often splitting it off whole. They don't mind if they shatter ore in the process - stone is most valuable to them, as they can craft a great many building materials from it.",

	"game:characterclass-spelunker": "Spelunker",
	"game:characterdesc-spelunker": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"Leave no stone unturned? That's what you said. Oh, you didn't mean it literally?\"\n</i></font><br><br>Spelunkers are prospectors and cavern explorers. They're always chasing the glimmer of precious metals and can find them with ease within rock and gravel alike, pickaxe in one hand and a pan in the other.",

	"game:characterclass-tailor": "Tailor",
	"game:characterdesc-tailor": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"We're cut from the same cloth? Well, one of us is going to have to change.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Tailors are weavers and clothiers. Given time, they can weave usable fibers from even the crudest grass, and then refine those fibers into a wide variety of clothing both practical and pretty for themselves and others to wear.",

	"game:characterclass-vintner": "Vintner",
	"game:characterdesc-vintner": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>\"Things get better with age? Uhm, yeah. Just look at me.\"\n</i></font><br><br>Vintners are winemakers and gatherers. While they appreciate the finer things in life, they can get by just fine by taking what they need from nature, something they often find themselves doing while waiting on drinks to ferment.",


